POST http://localhost:13000/workflows/quality-gate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "runId": "run-2026-09-17-001",
  "table": "silver.claims",
  "rowCount": 1048221,
  "rowCountDriftPct": 0.4,
  "nullRatePct": 0.2,
  "newColumns": [],
  "financialExposure": 40000,
  "containsSensitiveData": false,
  "isRegulatoryReporting": false
}

### Failing run - should suspend and wait for a steward (policy: drift + PII + $3M)
# Then open steward UI — no Elsa instance paste needed. Approve twice with different approver ids.
POST http://localhost:13000/workflows/quality-gate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "runId": "run-2026-09-17-002",
  "table": "silver.claims",
  "rowCount": 412008,
  "rowCountDriftPct": 61.7,
  "nullRatePct": 14.3,
  "newColumns": ["member_ssn"],
  "financialExposure": 3000000,
  "containsSensitiveData": true,
  "isRegulatoryReporting": true
}

### List pending (steward UI source)
GET http://localhost:5001/api/app/promotion/pending-list

### Approve #1 (two-person rule - not enough alone)
# Replace {id} with the request id from pending-list (field "id").
POST http://localhost:5001/api/app/promotion/{{id}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approverId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "approverTier": 3,
  "comment": "checked lineage"
}

### Approve #2 (reaches requiredApprovals=2)
POST http://localhost:5001/api/app/promotion/{{id}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approverId": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222",
  "approverTier": 3,
  "comment": "privacy reviewed"
}
